## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical data isolation, policy enforcement, and automated remediation in a multi-tenant AWS setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-prefix isolation in S3
- IAM condition keys (aws:SourceAccount, aws:SourceArn)
- Per-tenant KMS keys and grants
- Service Controls Policies to prevent cross-tenant writes
- Config-based drift detection and EventBridge-backed remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example bucket resource policy (conceptual)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::TENANT_ACCOUNT:role/TenantIngress"},
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-prefix-*/**",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:prefix": "tenant-prefix-*"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

